// WireMerge.rc
//
// Windows resource script. Embeds WireMerge.ico into the compiled .exe so
// Windows has an icon to show in the taskbar, window titlebar, Alt-Tab
// switcher, and File Explorer -- all pulled from this one embedded
// resource, no separate work needed per location.
//
// "IDI_ICON1" is just a symbolic resource name/ID -- Dear ImGui's Win32
// backend (main.cpp's WNDCLASSEXW setup) references it by string
// "IDI_ICON1" when setting hIcon/hIconSm, so the name here and the name
// used in main.cpp must match exactly.
//
// Compiled by windres (ships with MinGW-w64), NOT the C++ compiler --
// CMakeLists.txt is responsible for routing this file to windres instead
// of g++.
//
// ICON REVISION MARKER -- read this before replacing WireMerge.ico:
// Ninja/CMake's incremental build only re-invokes windres when THIS FILE
// (WireMerge.rc) changes -- windres does not emit a depfile the way gcc
// does for #include, so the build graph has no way to know the .ico
// referenced BELOW ever changed on its own. Swapping WireMerge.ico's
// bytes without touching this file can leave a STALE compiled resource
// object silently relinked into the .exe on an incremental build, with
// the OLD icon still embedded despite the new .ico sitting right there
// on disk. Bump the number below every time WireMerge.ico's actual
// pixel content changes, so this file's own content changes too and
// Ninja is forced to notice and recompile.
// icon-content-revision: 4 -- reverted back to the first logo asset
// (tightly-cropped WM cable mark, transparent background, small-size
// sharpened) after the full-bleed gradient version.

IDI_ICON1 ICON "WireMerge.ico"
